📘 Vivado Simulation Environment — AXI‑Full Backend
(Directory: parser_axi_full/sim/vivado/core/)

Overview
This directory contains the Vivado XSIM simulation environment for the AXI‑Full backend of the DexterLab parser system.

The simulation validates:

the AXI‑Full backend (cmd_axi_full.vhd)

integration with the parser core (cmd_parser.vhd and related packages)

AXI‑Full burst handling (INCR, FIFO, WRAP)

multi‑beat write and read sequences

AXI channel behavior (AW, W, B, AR, R)

the complete AXI testbench (tb_axi.vhd)

This README explains how to run the simulation.
For architectural details and protocol documentation, refer to the main project documentation under docs/.

Requirements
Windows 10/11

Vivado 2025.1 installed

settings64.bat available in the Vivado installation directory

MSYS2 / MINGW64 (optional, for Make)

Environment Setup
Before running any simulation, the Vivado environment must be activated.

Run:

Codice
xsim_env.bat
This script loads settings64.bat and prepares the Vivado toolchain (xvhdl, xelab, xsim).

Running the Simulation
Full simulation (compile + elaborate + run)
Codice
make xsim
This performs:

RTL compilation (xvhdl)

Testbench compilation (xvhdl)

Design elaboration (xelab)

Batch simulation (xsim)

The following files are generated:

xsim.dir/ — XSIM working directory

tb_axi_sim.wdb — waveform database

xsim.log, xelab.log — log files

Opening the GUI
To open the XSIM waveform viewer:

Codice
make xsim_gui
or manually:

Codice
xsim tb_axi_sim --gui
The GUI requires:

xsim.dir/

tb_axi_sim.wdb

Debug Logging
Debug messages (severity note) are controlled by:

vhdl
constant ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG : boolean := false;
located in:

Codice
cmd_cfg.vhd
Debug OFF (default)
suppresses all debug prints

warnings, errors, and fatals remain active

Debug ON
Set:

vhdl
ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG := true;
Vivado/XSIM does not support severity filtering, so debug control is implemented directly in VHDL.

Cleaning the Directory
To remove generated files:

Codice
make clean
This clears:

.Xil/

xsim.dir/

.log, .jou, .pb, .wdb files

Additional Documentation
For complete information about:

parser architecture

command semantics

AXI‑Full protocol behavior

burst/fifo/wrap handling

integration guidelines

refer to the documentation located in the docs/ directory of the parser_axi_full project.

